<speak>That is a clear administrative preference. A label describing the purpose can be more useful than one naming the person, particularly in a shared office. You could also choose a regular point in the day to collect that tray, so nobody needs to chase you with an envelope as you are heading into a meeting. For correspondence from the bank, are you finding the digital inbox convenient to access, or do you tend to leave it until you are at home? I am asking about the practical experience of using it, not about anything within the documents themselves.</speak>